legacy + with use_padding = false: values: true
%cd ~logic window 2*i<+k: extent: true
%cd ~logic window 2*i<+k: values: true
d/da of the strided dilated window: true
d/dw of the strided dilated window: true
d/da of the stride-and-offset scatter: true
result offset equal to the stride: affine axis `2*i+2` in einsum spec "s, i => s, 2*i+2" has offset 2, which is not smaller than its stride 2: the axis's extent is stride * n for an extent n of the strided label, so the last positions would fall outside it. Write an offset below the stride; to shift by whole strides, slice or pad the tensor separately.
result offset equal to the stride: refused at construction, naming the affine axis 2*i+2: true
result offset past the stride: refused at construction, naming the affine axis 2*i+5: true
result offset at stride 1, %op: refused at construction, naming the affine axis 1*i+1: true
result offset at stride 1, binary: refused at construction, naming the affine axis 1*i+1: true
result unpadded window with an offset: affine axis `2*i<+1+k` in einsum spec "s, i; k => s, 2*i<+1+k" has offset 1, which an unpadded (<+) window cannot take: its extent, stride * (n - 1) + the dilated kernel extent, has no room for an offset, so the last kernel positions would fall outside it. Drop the offset, and slice or pad the tensor separately to shift it.
result unpadded window with an offset: refused at construction, naming the affine axis 2*i<+1+k: true
result unpadded stride-1 window with an offset: refused at construction, naming the affine axis i<+1+k: true
result window with an offset, ternary: refused at construction, naming the affine axis i<+2+k: true
result offset, %cd ~logic: refused at construction, naming the affine axis 2*i<+1+k: true
operand offset equal to the stride: refused at construction, naming the affine axis 2*o+2: true
operand unpadded window with an offset: refused at construction, naming the affine axis 2*o<+1+k: true
the %op route of 2*o=+1+k has the plain string's extent: true
the %op route of 2*o=+1+k computes the plain string's values: true
